From 4630aae82aa0a31d35d4820a24df9e364a1e4477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:07:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a fieldset lays its rendered legend out outside
 its content

HTML renders a fieldset as its rendered legend (its first legend child, if
neither floated nor absolutely positioned) and an anonymous fieldset content
box holding the rest, which takes the fieldset's display, its flex and grid
container properties and its padding. Blitz laid the legend out as one more
child: in a flex fieldset it was a flex item, stretched and followed by the
gap, and in any fieldset it sat inside the padding.

Construction now gives such a fieldset two layout children, the legend and
an anonymous content box styled from the fieldset, and the fieldset lays
them out in a flow root of its own with no padding. A restyle of the
fieldset gives the content box that style again. The UA sheet makes the
rendered legend as wide as its content.
---
